:"நடுநாள்","parts":[{"text":"நடு","lemma":"நடு","gloss":"middle"},{"text":"நாள்","lemma":"நாள்","gloss":"night"}],"gloss":"midnight"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நல்","parts":[{"text":"நல்","lemma":"நல்","gloss":"good"}],"gloss":"good"},{"surface":"ஏறு","parts":[{"text":"ஏறு","lemma":"ஏறு","gloss":"bull"}],"gloss":"bull"},{"surface":"இயங்கு","parts":[{"text":"இயங்கு","lemma":"இயங்கு","gloss":"move"}],"gloss":"moving"},{"surface":"தோறு","parts":[{"text":"தோறு","lemma":"தோறு","gloss":"whenever"}],"gloss":"whenever"},{"surface":"இயம்பும்","parts":[{"text":"இயம்பு","lemma":"இயம்பு","gloss":"sound"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"relative participle suffix"}],"gloss":"that rings"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பல்","parts":[{"text":"பல்","lemma":"பல்","gloss":"many"}],"gloss":"many"},{"surface":"ஆன்","parts":[{"text":"ஆன்","lemma":"ஆன்","gloss":"cows"}],"gloss":"cows","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தொழுவத்து","parts":[{"text":"தொழுவத்து","lemma":"தொழுவத்து","gloss":"in the cowshed"}],"gloss":"in the cowshed","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"ஒரு","parts":[{"text":"ஒரு","lemma":"ஒரு","gloss":"single"}],"gloss":"a single"},{"surface":"மணி","parts":[{"text":"மணி","lemma":"மணி","gloss":"bell"}],"gloss":"bell"},{"surface":"குரலே","parts":[{"text":"குரல்","lemma":"குரல்","gloss":"sound"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis particle"}],"gloss":"the sound indeed"}]}],"literal":"Having caressed the broad shoulders with wavy dark hair, / he who departed for the sake of acquiring wealth, making tight bangles slip, / will he know, may you live long, O friend! The spotted, striped / cruel, angry snake's hooded head to be severed, / mighty thunder roars in the middle of the dark midnight, / whenever the good bull moves, there rings / in the cowshed of many cows, the sound of a single bell indeed!","translation":"O friend, may you live long! Will he—who caressed my broad shoulders and my wavy, dark hair, and then departed to acquire wealth, causing my tight bangles to slip off—ever know of this? In the deep darkness of midnight, when mighty thunder roars so fiercely that the hooded heads of spotted, striped, angry snakes are severed, there rings from the cowshed of many cows the sound of a single bell, whenever the fine bull moves.","modern":"தோழியே, நீ டூழி வாழ்க! அலை அலையான கரிய கூந்தலைத் தடவி, என் பருத்த தோள்களை நீவிவிட்டு, என் இறுக்கமான வளையல்கள் கழன்று வீழுமாறு பொருள் தேடுவதற்காகப் பிரிந்து சென்றாரே, அவர் அறிவாரோ? புள்ளிகளும் வரிகளும் உடைய கொடிய கோபங்கொண்ட பாம்புகளின் படம் பொருந்திய தலைகள் துண்டாகி விழும்படி, வலிமையான இடி முழங்குகின்ற நள்ளிரவு நேரத்தில், பல பசுக்கள் கட்டப்பட்டுள்ள தொழுவத்தில், நல்ல காளை மாடு அசையும் போதெல்லாம் ஒலிக்கின்ற அந்த ஒற்றை மணியின் ஓசையை அவர் அறிவாரோ?","explanation":"This poem is set in the Mullai landscape, which represents patient waiting during the rainy season. The heroine is speaking to her close friend about her deep distress over the hero's prolonged absence. He had departed to earn wealth, promising to return before the rains, but has not yet arrived. The rainy season has now set in, marked by terrifying midnight thunder that is said to shatter the hoods of angry snakes. In the quiet, dark night, the only sound is the single bell tied to the leading bull in the cowshed, ringing whenever it moves. This lonely sound intensifies the heroine's grief, and she wonders if her lover, far away, has any idea of the torment she undergoes in the dark hours.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}